        <dd><a href="https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D028723.html">
            http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D028723
        </a></dd>

        <span id="annotation">
            <dt>Annotation</dt><dd>do not confuse with <a href="/record/ui?ui=D007206" class="textLink_INDIVIDUALITY">INDIVIDUALITY</a></dd>
        </span>
                <span id="scopeNote">
                    <dt>Scope Note</dt><dd>The state or condition of being a human individual accorded moral and/or legal rights. Criteria to be used to determine this status are subject to debate, and range from the requirement of simply being a human organism to such requirements as that the individual be self-aware and capable of rational thought and moral agency.</dd>
                </span>
            
                <dt>Previous Indexing</dt>
                
                    <dd>Individuality (1974-2001)</dd>
                
                <dt>See Also</dt>
                
                    <dd><a id="seeAlso_BeginningofHumanLife"
                           href="/record/ui?ui=D033421"
                        >Beginning of Human Life</a></dd>
                
                    <dd><a id="seeAlso_HumanCharacteristics"
                           href="/record/ui?ui=D040821"
                        >Human Characteristics</a></dd>
                
            <dt>Public MeSH Note</dt><dd>2002; see INDIVIDUALITY 1995-2001</dd>
        
            <dt>History Note</dt><dd>2002; use INDIVIDUALITY 1995-2001</dd>
        
        


        
